LAST_SUCCESS=🎉 FIRST PIXEL: single-Color.red probe renders a real OpenSwiftUI DisplayList on wasm32-wasip1, clean exit 0: "fill x:0 y:0 w:640 h:480 #FF3B30FF" (SwiftUI system red, full surface). Full pipeline App->AppGraph->ViewGraph->AttributeGraph(Compute)->render->DisplayList works on wasm. Fix: exit(0) right after renderOnce in StdoutApp.swift (#if os(WASI)) sidesteps the teardown swiftcall trap (GraphHost.deinit->Subgraph.forEach) AND flushes stdout - render was always working.
NOTES=Strategy validated (2 agents+test): macro-flip general fix REJECTED empirically; shrink-probe + recognize teardown!=render delivered first pixel via 1-line exit(0) instead of C++ grind. NEXT for richer UIs: (1) Subgraph.forEach/AGSubgraphApply *C variant (validate in 4s harness repros/compute-wasm/computerun) for clean teardown + mid-render forEach; (2) swift_conformsToProtocol C-shim in OpenSwiftUI_SPI (for VStack/TupleView); (3) bounded Compute set AGGraphReadCachedAttribute/Search/TupleWithBuffer/AGTypeApplyEnumData/MutableEnumData. Phase 4 = wire DisplayList->Option-B CGContext drawer (repros/swift-canvas-spike) -> device. ALL builds need ANY_ATTRIBUTE_FIX=0. Patches current: openswiftui-phase1-wip(+StdoutApp exit), oag-fork, compute-wasm. probe=Color.red.
